                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Eight months into my term as a U.S. Representative, I understand a simple truth: you can\u2019t legislate from behind a desk. To make informed, effective policy on wildfire preparedness, forest health, and public lands, you must walk the land, sometimes stumble over its roots, and hear directly from those doing the hard work on the ground.\n\nThat\u2019s why I\u2019m backpacking 40 miles around Mt. Hood. Over this four-day trek, I\u2019ll meet with Tribal leaders, conservationists, and policy partners to build durable policies that protect Mt. Hood\u2014and all our treasured places\u2014for generations to come.",
